          "quote": "Another distinct feature is bulging of grain boundaries to facilitate dynamic recrystallization. The grain boundary bulging is a common feature for materials deformed at high temperatures [ 67 ]. This GB bulging acts as stress reliever during deformation to accommodate steady state deformation without fracture as seen in current work at high temperatures.",
